I agree with Divij. A nightly Apache Kafka build for PowerPC would be we=
lcome. But it shouldn't run on every build, since the extra time and com=
plexity would not be worth it.

By the way, are there any features or plugins we don't intend to support=
 on PPC? If there are, this KIP would be a good place to spell them out.

Naively, I would think all of our Java and Scala code should work on PPC=
 without changes. However, there may be library dependencies that don't =
exist on PPC. (We have to remember that the last desktop PowerPC chip th=
at an average user could buy shipped in 2005....)

best,
Colin


