Hi Colin,

The way I understood Philp's message is that KIP-944 also plays nice=20
with KIP-945. But I might be mistaken.

Regardless, KIP-945 does /not/ resolve the underlying problem (the need=20
for nested consumer invocations) because it has the explicit goal of not=20
changing the user facing API.

 > ... KIP-945 but haven't posted a DISCUSS thread yet

There is a thread called 'KafkaConsumer refactor proposal', but indeed=20
no official discussion yet.

 > I really don't want to be debugging complex interactions between Java=20
thread-local variables and green threads.

In that email thread, I proposed an API change in which callbacks are no=20
longer needed. The proposal completely removes the need for such complex=20
interactions. In addition, it gives clients the ability to process at=20
full speed even while a coorperative rebalance is ongoing.

Regards,
 =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 Erik.

