David Mao created KAFKA-15192:
---------------------------------

             Summary: Network thread receives exception when updating reque=
st metrics
                 Key: KAFKA-15192
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15192
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: metrics
            Reporter: David Mao


We noticed an exception being thrown from the network threads when updating=
 some of the request histograms. Example stack trace:

=C2=A0
java.util.NoSuchElementException
=09at java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentSkipListMap.firstKey(ConcurrentSkipLis=
tMap.java:2064)
=09at com.yammer.metrics.stats.ExponentiallyDecayingSample.update(Exponenti=
allyDecayingSample.java:102)
=09at com.yammer.metrics.stats.ExponentiallyDecayingSample.update(Exponenti=
allyDecayingSample.java:81)
=09at com.yammer.metrics.core.Histogram.update(Histogram.java:110)
=C2=A0

Searching the error I found a similar ticket resolved in Cassandra by updat=
ing their dropwizard dependency to pull in [https://github.com/dropwizard/m=
etrics/pull/1436]. https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CASSANDRA-15472

Kafka currently still uses yammer metrics, so we would need to take [https:=
//cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-510%3A+Metrics+library+upgr=
ade] forward to upgrade to a dropwizard version that fixes this issue.



