Hi Colin, Philip, Kirk,

As far as I am aware all concerns about KIP-944 have been addressed.=20
Including those about dirty reads between threads and green threads=20
because of missing memory barriers. If you agree, I would like to open=20
the vote again. If not, please let me know.

I'll open another KIP with a proposal on how to improve the consumer API=20
so that we don't need any thread trickery anymore. I would rather not=20
wait for that one because there will be a lot work before that can even=20
be implemented.

Once KIP-944 has been accepted, I'll work on adding the unit tests that=20
are described in the KIP.

Kind regards,
 =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 Erik.


Op 30-06-2023 om 07:56 schreef Erik van Oosten:
> [This is a resend with the correct KIP number.]
>
> Hello developers of the Java based consumer,
>
> I submitted https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/13914 to fix a long=20
> standing problem that the Kafka consumer on the JVM is not usable from=20
> asynchronous runtimes such as Kotlin co-routines and ZIO. However,=20
> since it extends the public API I was requested to create a KIP.
>
> So here it is:
> KIP-944 Support async runtimes in consumer=20
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/chw0Dw
>
> Any questions, comments, ideas and other additions are welcome!
>
> The KIP should be complete except for the testing section. As far as I=20
> am aware there are no tests for the current behavior. Any help in this=20
> area would be appreciated.
>
> Kind regards,
> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 Erik.
>
>
--=20
Erik van Oosten
e.vanoosten@grons.nl
https://day-to-day-stuff.blogspot.com


