Hi Hamza,
TLS for Kafka is not implemented in any significantly different way =
compared to other TLS-enabled services. A good place to start with is =
the Apache Kafka documentation:

https://kafka.apache.org/090/documentation.html#security_ssl=EF=BF=BC
Apache Kafka
kafka.apache.org

You=E2=80=99ll find a lot of other resources out there that explain TLS =
and PKI, it=E2=80=99s not really a topic that can be addressed on the =
dev mailing list. If you have a specific question on how TLS works in =
Kafka I=E2=80=99d recommend asking on the user mailing list =
(users@kafka.apache.org), but I would strongly recommend reading up on =
TLS itself first.

Kind regards,
Jim


