Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=flowed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hello developers of the Java consumer,

This is a simpler alternative to KIP-944 as proposed by Chris Egerton.

In this proposal we make method acquire and release of the KafkaConsumer=20
class protected. This allows anyone to implement these methods as=20
appropriate for their environment.

The wiki page for KIP-957 contains more details=20
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/lY6zDw

This is a call for discussion. If possible I would like to include this=20
change in Kafka 3.6.
Any questions, comments, ideas and other additions are welcome!

Kind regards,
 =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 Erik.


