We embed the Kafka client=C2=A0 in IBM App Connect Enterprise in order to p=
rovide Kafka consume and=C2=A0 produce functionality. This product is a lit=
tle=C2=A0 bit like an app server in that it may host multiple workloads inc=
luding some which may not use the Kafka functionality.

=C2=A0

When the Kafka server is installed in an open shift environment we are seei=
ng cases where the clients receive OutOfMemory errors due to single large (=
1.2Gb) byte buffers being allocated by the client.

=C2=A0

>From research this appears to be a known issue when a plaintext client is c=
onfigured to attempt connection to a TLS secured endpoint however in this i=
nstance we see successful communication=C2=A0 via TLS and then when the Kaf=
ka server is restarted (or connectivity is broken) both the consumers and p=
roducers can throw OutOfMemoryError's with the following stacks:

