Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-15263) KRaftMigrationDriver can run the
 migration twice
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

David Arthur created KAFKA-15263:
------------------------------------

             Summary: KRaftMigrationDriver can run the migration twice
                 Key: KAFKA-15263
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15263
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: David Arthur
            Assignee: David Arthur


There is a narrow race condition in KRaftMigrationDriver where a PollEvent =
can run that sees the internal state as ZK_MIGRATION and is immediately fol=
lowed by another poll event (due to external call to {{{}wakeup(){}}}) that=
 results in two=C2=A0MigrateMetadataEvent being enqueued.=C2=A0

Since MigrateMetadataEvent lacks a check on the internal state, this causes=
 the metadata migration to occur twice.=C2=A0



--
